Optionally correct the antenna period error of the centroid (TipSignalReference, CellCorrection*, CentroidFadeMin/Max)

The position between two antennas is interpolated from three amplitudes, and neither the parabola
nor the centroid is linear in the true position: a slow straight diagonal stroke comes out wavy,
once per antenna. Measured on the Surface Pro 9 with the Slim Pen 2 on strokes drawn along a
straight edge (deviation from the fitted line, split into the part that repeats with the X and
with the Y antennas, amplitude in mm on that axis):

- parabola on X, centroid on Y: X 0.09 at 20 degrees of tilt and light pressure, 0.26 .. 0.35 at
  45 degrees, 0.45 on a very slow stroke at 40 degrees with firm pressure (plus 0.32 twice per
  antenna, where a neighbour antenna in antiphase pins the parabola to the cell border for a third
  of the cell); Y 0.06 .. 0.24.
- centroid on both axes: X 0.04 .. 0.28, Y 0.05 .. 0.23, almost only the first harmonic.

Nothing else contributes: the tilt offset and its smoothing add 0.002 .. 0.013 mm, the jitter lock
0 .. 0.014 mm, and the two MPP v2 position windows agree.

The error of the centroid follows the strength of the tip signal (which grows with pressure and
tilt), not the tilt or the pressure alone: its cosine part goes from +0.05 mm at the signal level
of light writing through zero to -0.27 mm at 1.7 times that level, the same on both axes. With

  level = summed amplitude of the three antennas, mean of both axes / TipSignalReference
  error = (Cos + CosLevel (level - 1)) cos(2 pi x) + (Sin + SinLevel (level - 1)) sin(2 pi x)
        + Cos2 cos(4 pi x) + Sin2 sin(4 pi x)                      (x and error in antennas)

subtracted from the centroid (per axis: CellCorrectionCosX .. CellCorrectionSin2Y, level limited
to CellCorrectionLevelMin .. Max), the same strokes give X 0.003 .. 0.030 mm and Y 0.008 ..
0.034 mm, and the deviation from the line falls from 0.07 .. 0.35 mm rms to 0.02 .. 0.07 mm, which
is what the hand contributes. With the coefficients fitted without the group of strokes that is
evaluated: 0.005 .. 0.045 mm per axis at levels of 1.2 and more, 0.05 .. 0.06 mm at level 1.0
(two strokes; without the correction 0.06 .. 0.09 mm there). The coefficients are a least squares
fit to 14 strokes at four combinations of tilt and pressure, all with the pen leaning to the lower
right; light upright writing and other leaning directions are not covered by a measurement.

The correction applies where the centroid is selected (PositionCentroidX / Y), needs no state and
adds no delay. Everything else of a sample is unchanged.

CentroidFadeMin / CentroidFadeMax: with a weak signal (pen hovering high) the centroid jumps, one
position in ten is off by 0.4 .. 1.3 mm from its neighbours where the parabola is off by 0.14 ..
0.28 mm. Below CentroidFadeMin (in units of TipSignalReference) the parabola is used, above
CentroidFadeMax the centroid, in between a mix.

All off by default.

